data: {"level":1,"reviewed":{"level":1,"label":"concept","text":"The sampler never sees the logits directly. It sees one probability vector, which is built in\nstages: first the temperature reshapes the scores, then top-k removes low-ranked tokens, then\ntop-p removes the tail of the ranking. After each removal the rest must be rescaled so the mass\nsums to one. Each stage is a mask followed by a renormalisation."},"hints_note":null}

